error[B0217]: `same` is declared twice
 --> check/overloads.bloom:6:13
  |
6 | public func same(x: String) -> String { x }
  |             ^^^^ a second declaration
  |
help: overloads are told apart by their argument labels, not their types: give one other labels, or rename it
  = docs: https://github.com/OxyHQ/Bloom/blob/main/docs/bloom-lang-spec.mdx#10-modules-and-interop

error[B0202]: `go` is overloaded: name one by its labels
 --> check/overloads.bloom:9:11
  |
9 |   let f = go
  |           ^^ more than one function has this name
  |
help: call one of `go(by:)`, `go(with:)`
  = docs: https://github.com/OxyHQ/Bloom/blob/main/docs/bloom-lang-spec.mdx#5-values-functions-and-closures

error[B0207]: no `go` takes the labels `(at:)`
  --> check/overloads.bloom:10:10
   |
10 |   return go(at: 1) + pick()
   |          ^^ not one of its overloads
   |
help: its overloads are `go(by:)`, `go(with:)`
   = docs: https://github.com/OxyHQ/Bloom/blob/main/docs/bloom-lang-spec.mdx#5-values-functions-and-closures

error[B0207]: this call of `pick` is ambiguous
  --> check/overloads.bloom:10:22
   |
10 |   return go(at: 1) + pick()
   |                      ^^^^ more than one overload takes these labels
   |
help: `pick(a:)`, `pick(b:)` all fit: write the labels of one in full
